From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 03:50:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] protected-wins: carry registrations across the W1 rebase and
 register the unregistered measured wins (Sol REJECT fix 3)

Validate on the candidate went from 83 problems to 2. Pre-rebase arifi/main e86ca0289 already failed with 27 of them (receipt pw-validate-prerebase-e86ca0289.txt), so most of this is debt the W1 rebase inherited, not debt it created.

1. replay-provenance.json: 37 rebased commits mapped to their registered originals via replay-map against the retained tag arifi-pre-rebase-e86ca0289 (patch-id, trailers and subject re-derived live).
2. 13 registered wins whose patch-id changed only by context (-U0 patch-id equal) or by the f172be756 file split (changed-line multiset identical) now name their rebased sha; the original moves to commit_pre_rebase_chain, re-homed files join protected_paths, and each carries a _rebase_b11178 line naming the check.
3. 14 new entries register the 27 inherited unregistered wins (R48, R48b, R52b, R53, R57, R58, R61, R64, R65, R71, R75, R85, R87) and lane-296's own N11/N12 width rule (695de319a, c1848cbb4, 10ce09fd6, 76a5fd303). OW-028 attaches to vulkan-rocmfp4-fast-q8_1-mmvq. Every field is taken from the originating commit body or lane report; entries whose effect was a tie or a loss say so.

Still unregistered (2): d244e72fe (g128 Vulkan port, content-edited by the upstream pipeline map) and 115f9e3f9 (DFlash fused/legacy switch, content-edited by the llama_batch_ext re-home). Their registered gates are GPU legs, owed in the lane-296 Sol-fix GPU run.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-296 Sol-fix pass, Opus 5.5)
Measured-effect: none - registry only
